Tested ACK 959081325d

Benchmarked GetPubKeyFromInput on 2-of-3 multisig P2SH: drops from 1191 to 94 cycles on Zen 2 (-O2). All bip352_tests pass.

Since `interpreter.cpp:2092` requires `scriptSig == CScript() << redeem`, any valid P2SH-P2WPKH scriptSig is always a single push of the 22-byte program (`[22, OP_0, 20, <hash>]`, 23 bytes total). Could skip `EvalScript` and `Solver` entirely:

```diff
-        std::vector<std::vector<unsigned char>> stack;
-        if (!EvalScript(stack, txin.scriptSig, SCRIPT_VERIFY_NONE, DUMMY_CHECKER, SigVersion::BASE)) {
-            return std::nullopt;
-        }
-        if (stack.empty()) return std::nullopt;
-        CScript redeem{stack.back().begin(), stack.back().end()};
-        if (Solver(redeem, solutions) != TxoutType::WITNESS_V0_KEYHASH) return std::nullopt;
+        if (txin.scriptSig.size() != 23 ||
+            txin.scriptSig[0] != 22 ||
+            txin.scriptSig[1] != OP_0 ||
+            txin.scriptSig[2] != WITNESS_V0_KEYHASH_SIZE) {
+            return std::nullopt;
+        }
```

That also avoids `EvalScript` when the witness is non-empty (P2SH-P2WSH drops from 357 to 131 cycles), and removes the interpreter dependency on `CScriptWitness` ahead of #36521. Fine either way.

